  "description": "Version 2 terms under the gpu-reservation/1 template. Canonical JSON is RFC 8785 with bigints as decimal strings, writing non-ASCII characters as UTF-8 without escaping them. The arbiter's address is written in lower case before the resolution section is hashed, whatever case the terms hold it in. Each section salt is HKDF-SHA256 of the commitment salt, with no HKDF salt, info \"avow:terms:v2:salt:<section>\" and 32 bytes out. Each section hash is keccak256(abi.encode(string \"avow:terms:v2:<section>\", bytes32 sectionSalt, string canonicalJson)). The terms hash is keccak256(abi.encode(string \"avow:terms:v2\", string headerJson, bytes32 subject, bytes32 consideration, bytes32 remedies, bytes32 resolution, bytes32 backing)). lockTerms is what Avow's approval carries for a 6-decimal token.",
